-- title:
--   Newform eigenplane not inside the finite part of Tₚ J₀(N₀p)
-- statement:
--   Fix $N_0\neq 0$ and a prime $p$ with $p\nmid N_0$, a valuation subring $A$ of an algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $A$, level data $\Lambda$ for $(N_0,p,A)$ satisfying `IsJacobian`, and a Néron object $O$ over these data; assume that for every $m>0$, every $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ and every $m$-torsion point $x$ of $J_0(N_0p)$ one has $\sigma\cdot x-x\in O.\mathrm{finPts}\,m$, the subgroup generated by the $m$-torsion points whose associated section extends to a point over $\operatorname{Spec} A$. Let $g$ be a weight-$2$ cusp form on $\Gamma_0(N_0p)$ which is a newform in the project's sense, let $S$ be a finite set of naturals containing $p$ and every prime divisor of $N_0p$, let $O'$ be a complete discrete valuation ring of characteristic zero with finite residue field and $p$ in its maximal ideal, let $\chi_g$ be a ring homomorphism from the Hecke algebra of level $N_0p$, weight $2$ and excluded set $S\setminus\{p\}$ to $\mathbb{C}$ sending $T_\ell$ to the $\ell$-th $q$-coefficient of $g$ for primes $\ell\nmid N_0p$ outside $S\setminus\{p\}$, and let $\iota$ map the range of $\chi_g$ into $O'$. Let $O''$ be a further such ring, finite and local over $O'$ and a $\mathbb{Z}_p$-algebra, with fraction field $K$. Using the Hecke module structure `heckeModuleBar` on $J_0(N_0p)$, consider a $\mathbb{Z}_p$-module structure on the Tate module $T=\mathrm{TateModule}\,p\,(J_0(N_0p))$ acting on each coordinate through $\mathbb{Z}/p^n$, a monoid homomorphism $\rho_M$ from $\operatorname{Gal}$ to $\operatorname{End}_{O''}(O''\otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_p}T)$ and a ring homomorphism $T_M$ from [`ModularCurve.HeckeAlg`](def/HeckeGalois_EichlerShimura.html#L14) to the same endomorphism ring, both compatible with the coordinatewise Galois and Hecke actions, and a $K$-submodule $W$ of $K\otimes_{O''}(O''\otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_p}T)$ of rank $2$ which is stable under the base changes of $\rho_M$, on which $T_\ell$ acts by the scalar image of $a_\ell(g)$ and all Frobenius elements at $\ell$ have trace that scalar, for primes $\ell\nmid N_0p$ outside $S$, and on which the generator of `HeckeAlg` at $p$ acts by the scalar image of the Hecke algebra element $U_p$. The conclusion is that $W$ is not contained in the $K$-span of the elements $1\otimes(1\otimes x)$ with $x\in T$ such that $x_n\in O.\mathrm{finPts}\,(p^n)$ for all $n$.
--
--   This is the non-degeneracy input in Ribet's level-lowering argument at a prime $p$ exactly dividing the level: the two-dimensional eigenplane attached to a newform of level $N_0p$ meets the finite (non-toric) part of the $p$-adic Tate module only in a line, so it cannot lie inside it. It is used in [`CuspForm.IsNewform.frobenius_sub_heckeU_smul_mem_monodromySpan_eigenPlane_tateModule_jZero_of_dvd`](thm.html#CuspForm.IsNewform.frobenius_sub_heckeU_smul_mem_monodromySpan_eigenPlane_tateModule_jZero_of_dvd), which extracts from this the monodromy relation between Frobenius and $U_p$ on the eigenplane.
